  "source": "PiTheory original",
  "question": "In a simple pendulum experiment, the length is measured as $1.000\\ \\text{m}$ with an error of $1\\ \\text{mm}$, and the time period as $2.00\\ \\text{s}$ with an error of $0.02\\ \\text{s}$. Find the maximum percentage error in the value of $g$.",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [],
  "answer": "",
  "numerical_answer": "2.1",
  "tolerance": "0.05",
  "solution": "$g = \\dfrac{4\\pi^2 L}{T^2}$, so\n$$\\frac{\\Delta g}{g}\\times 100 = \\frac{\\Delta L}{L}\\times 100 + 2\\,\\frac{\\Delta T}{T}\\times 100$$\n$$= \\frac{0.001}{1.000}\\times 100 + 2\\times\\frac{0.02}{2.00}\\times 100 = 0.1\\% + 2\\% = 2.1\\%$$",
